<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Sks on Exoscale Academy</title><link>https://layer5io.github.io/exoscale-academy/pr-preview/pr-372/tags/sks/</link><description>Recent content in Sks on Exoscale Academy</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><atom:link href="https://layer5io.github.io/exoscale-academy/pr-preview/pr-372/tags/sks/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Creating SKS Cluster</title><link>https://layer5io.github.io/exoscale-academy/pr-preview/pr-372/learning-paths/1e2a8e46-937c-47ea-ab43-5716e3bcab2e/end-to-end-kubernetes/practice-on-exoscale/practice/exoscale-managed-kubernetes/content/creating-sks-cluster/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://layer5io.github.io/exoscale-academy/pr-preview/pr-372/learning-paths/1e2a8e46-937c-47ea-ab43-5716e3bcab2e/end-to-end-kubernetes/practice-on-exoscale/practice/exoscale-managed-kubernetes/content/creating-sks-cluster/</guid><description>&lt;p>SKS (Scalable Kubernetes Service) is the Exoscale-managed cluster. To deploy an SKS cluster, we can use one of the
following tools:&lt;/p>
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>&lt;a href="https://terraform.com">Terraform&lt;/a>&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;a href="https://pulumi.com">Pulumi&lt;/a>&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;a href="https://github.com/exoscale/cli">exo cli&lt;/a>&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;a href="https://exoscale.com">Exoscale Portal&lt;/a>&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;p>Whatever tool we use, it creates the following resources:&lt;/p>
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>a Security Group and some associated rules&lt;/li>
&lt;li>an SKS cluster&lt;/li>
&lt;li>a Nodepool&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;p>We will go through the details of each approach, so you can select the one you prefer. But first, you need to create an account and get free credits to follow this workshop.&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>SKS Welcome</title><link>https://layer5io.github.io/exoscale-academy/pr-preview/pr-372/learning-paths/1e2a8e46-937c-47ea-ab43-5716e3bcab2e/end-to-end-kubernetes/sks-advance/welcome/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://layer5io.github.io/exoscale-academy/pr-preview/pr-372/learning-paths/1e2a8e46-937c-47ea-ab43-5716e3bcab2e/end-to-end-kubernetes/sks-advance/welcome/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Concepts</title><link>https://layer5io.github.io/exoscale-academy/pr-preview/pr-372/learning-paths/1e2a8e46-937c-47ea-ab43-5716e3bcab2e/end-to-end-kubernetes/sks-advance/concepts/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://layer5io.github.io/exoscale-academy/pr-preview/pr-372/learning-paths/1e2a8e46-937c-47ea-ab43-5716e3bcab2e/end-to-end-kubernetes/sks-advance/concepts/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Containers</title><link>https://layer5io.github.io/exoscale-academy/pr-preview/pr-372/learning-paths/1e2a8e46-937c-47ea-ab43-5716e3bcab2e/end-to-end-kubernetes/sks-starter/containers/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://layer5io.github.io/exoscale-academy/pr-preview/pr-372/learning-paths/1e2a8e46-937c-47ea-ab43-5716e3bcab2e/end-to-end-kubernetes/sks-starter/containers/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Scalable Kubernetes Services (SKS) Starter</title><link>https://layer5io.github.io/exoscale-academy/pr-preview/pr-372/learning-paths/1e2a8e46-937c-47ea-ab43-5716e3bcab2e/end-to-end-kubernetes/sks-starter/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://layer5io.github.io/exoscale-academy/pr-preview/pr-372/learning-paths/1e2a8e46-937c-47ea-ab43-5716e3bcab2e/end-to-end-kubernetes/sks-starter/</guid><description/></item><item><tit